{
  "about": "Surface-value rules for surface.py, by country: how a postcode is shaped and which range a city sits in, how a landline and a mobile are formatted and which area code a city carries, which registration-number scheme a business carries (checksums are computed in code, only the body is drawn), and what a bank account looks like. Country names match the second half of each locale's (city, country) pairs. Patterns: '#' is a drawn digit, '@' is the city's area code. Versioned, and every version is KEPT: `versions` maps a version number to the complete rule set that was current under it, and `current` names the one a new build uses. A change to any rule is a new entry, never an edit to an existing one, because a corpus records the version it was built under (`master_data.identifiers`) and replays under exactly those rules — an old version that changed would move every postcode in every corpus that carries it.",
